@startuml
title DASHI TOE — fleet formal-gap target boundary

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "External planning receipt" {
  component "ITIR-suite R4/R5 context\n584 discharged\n44 contradiction gaps\n58 formal gaps\n3 eigen motifs" as FleetContext
}

package "Existing DASHI owners" {
  component "PNFSpectralCoordinateRebuildability" as Rebuild
  component "PNFSpectralNumericABICore" as Numeric
  component "PNFResidualFieldInvariants" as Residual
  component "PlanningPNFClaimBoundaryExact" as Planning
  component "Promotion.ObligationIndex" as Obligation
  component "Balaban/Ibrahim Pareto-Snowball TOE" as Pareto
}

package "Normalized DASHI/Unified surface" {
  component "FleetFormalGapTargetTOEExact" as Facade
  component "FleetFormalGapTargetTOEValidation" as Validation
}

package "TOE consumers" {
  component "EverythingTOESymmetryResolved369" as TOE
  component "Unifier" as Unifier
  component "Unified.Everything" as Unified
}

FleetContext ..> Facade : external planning values only
Rebuild --> Facade
Numeric --> Facade
Residual --> Facade
Planning --> Facade
Obligation --> Facade
Pareto --> Facade : O/R/C/S/L/P/G/F carrier

Facade --> TOE
Facade --> Unifier
TOE --> Validation
Unifier --> Validation
Validation --> Unified

note bottom of Facade
Preconditions:
- external R4/R5 receipt is context, not proof authority
- canonical DASHI owners remain theorem authority
- ESD surfaces remain read-only

Invariants:
- target only 58 unformalised formal gaps
- 584 discharged fibres stay outside the target
- 44 contradiction gaps stay separate
- 3 eigen motifs set search priority only
- eigenvalue magnitude does not create proof
- external counts do not create discharge

Postconditions:
- TOE and Unifier expose the same owner receipt
- exact 58/584/44/3 values are regression-checked
- no ESD mutation
- no theorem ownership transfer
end note

@enduml
